          <p><strong><span data-num-exempt="the list's own numbering (a position)">3.</span> Severity</strong> — {% if zip_stats | default([]) %}each {{ area_label | default('ZIP') | e }} is ranked HIGH, MED or LOW by tertiles of the data's own primary metric.{% else %}this data has no per-area figures, so the dashboard shows its system-wide figures as given.{% endif %}</p>
          <p><strong><span data-num-exempt="the list's own numbering (a position)">4.</span> Rendering</strong> — one HTML page with the data embedded as JSON, charts drawn by Chart.js{% if chartjs_inline %} (inlined, so they need no network){% endif %}, and views that filter each other.</p>
          <p><strong><span data-num-exempt="the list's own numbering (a position)">5.</span> Curveball</strong> — {% if curveball_text %}this page is Block 2: {% if cb_block and cb_block.unchanged is not none %}Python compared every endpoint with Block 1's snapshot (listed under &ldquo;What changed at the curveball&rdquo;){% elif cb_block and cb_block.snapshot %}no Block 1 snapshot was found, so the data was not compared{% else %}no change list of this run was found, so the data was not compared{% endif %}; a resource the announcement names as closed in the same sentence is marked closed by the announcement; a record whose own status reads closed is marked closed by the data.{% else %}at the curveball this harness reads the change list Python computes (every endpoint compared with this run's snapshot), marks a resource closed when the announcement names it as closed in the same sentence, and lists what changed; a record whose own status reads closed is marked closed by the data in both blocks.{% endif %}</p>
          {% if chatbot_enabled %}<p><strong><span data-num-exempt="the list's own numbering (a position)">6.</span> Ask AI</strong> — the chat panel sends your question and this page's data summary to Claude through a server-side proxy; no key is on the page. Try: &ldquo;{{ domain_hints_chatbot | e }}&rdquo;</p>{% endif %}
        </div>
